<p>Hello Noname1810! lets take a look :)</p>
<p><strong>SAND</strong></p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p><strong>Quick note:</strong><br />
I noticed some grammar errors throughout the post, I would recommend double checking the spelling, as bad grammar can make it harder to understand and accurately critique concepts.</p>
<p><strong>The concept:</strong></p>
<blockquote>
<p>• SCP-xxxx is a working compass, observation outside the area of 200m radius from SCP-xxxx on the area within will result as if there is currently no SCP-xxxx and sapient being (having intelligence at least equal to lizards) inside the area. Observers from inside will perceive white fog at the border of the area which can't be seen through.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>It could just be me, but this confuses me a bit; &quot;sapient being (having intelligence at least equal to lizards) inside the area&quot;. Lizards would be much closer to sentient than sapient, as they aren't self aware and don't share the same complexity as humans (to my knowledge, the same goes for all animals). -are certain animals affected by this too, or is it only humans? if certain animals are affected, how does it relate back to the concept and narrative?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>• SCP-xxxx-1 is any sapient being that currently observing SCP-xxxx, other SCP-xxxx-1 or on SCP-xxxx-2<br />
• If there are about 11 to 35 SCP-xxxx-1 at the moment, SCP-xxxx might transfer all SCP-xxxx-1 along with everything thing in their sight and touch to the magnetic South Pole a planet designated as SCP-xxxx-2 in an unknown dimension. When in this area, if SCP-xxxx is destroyed or has a distance more than 10m away from all SCP-xxxx-1 and out of sight, SCP-xxxx will reappears within 10m of the closest SCP-xxxx-1.</p>
</blockquote>
<blockquote>
<p>• SCP-xxxx-2 has a diameter about 1100km, its surface is made up of places in and out side our dimension, those places are constantly changing when out of observation. Interaction on SCP-xxxx-2 affect those places where they come from (a record of expedition in SCP-xxxx-2 was found in an abandoned house). The only way known to get out of SCP-xxxx-2 is to put SCP-xxxx directly on the magnetic North Pole of the planet.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Currently, the concept feels directionless as there isn't much behind the initial effects and specific details. There also isn't any sort of explanation or purpose for the skips existence shown here, which makes it hard to get invested in the idea.</p>
<p>Along with this, the concept feels overcomplicated, as the skips effects only seem to manifest under fairly specific conditions. There are also other smaller ideas that are only semi-related to the main concept, that don't really add much. ie. the intelligence level of living beings, the north and south poles, the extra dimensional areas.</p>
<p>- Overall, I would recommend simplifying the concept down, try to get an idea of the core concept and trim off anything that doesn't contribute to the main idea.</p>
<p><strong>Some questions I got:</strong><br />
why is SCP-xxxx-2 made up of so many different places?<br />
why do those places change?<br />
why/how can you only get out SCP-xxxx-2 when the compass is put on the North pole?<br />
how do the different dimensions play a part in this?<br />
what is the white fog that occurs around the compass?<br />
why does the compass transport people to an extra dimensional space in certain circumstances?</p>
<p><strong>The narrative:</strong></p>
<blockquote>
<p>The foundation found SCP-xxxx after many report of missing in a small town, MTF team was sent in for investigation.<br />
• Expedition 1 summary:<br />
Upon recovering SCP-xxxx, it manifested and transferred 11 researchers and the MTF team to SCP-xxxx-2. After more than 2 years, they became the first people to exit SCP-xxxx-2.<br />
After that SCP-xxxx activated several times and caused lost of many personnel but SCP-xxxx didn’t activate while they tried to test it<br />
• Expedition 2 summary:<br />
Several guards, personnel and D-class was transferred by SCP-xxxx-2, they got out with loss of most people. This expedition gave the foundation a lot of valuable information.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>The setup is a little vague, as it doesn't show how the skip itself was found, or what happens immediately after.- Considering the skips anomaly isn't immediately obvious. -Where's the lead-up to the investigations and expeditions? why does the Foundation decide to look further into this?</p>
<p>The middle act, payoff and main conflict don't seem to be shown in the story, which makes the stories events feel flat, and closer to a few instances that don't have much correlation with each other. How should I feel about the story? why should I care about the characters? - Currently the entire narrative seems to be in the expedition logs, which alone won't be able to carry the article.</p>
<p>As for the expeditions themselves, there isn't much here showing actually happens, or much showing how and what the Foundation finds out about the skip. Considering the exploration will play a major role in the narrative, I would recommend showing what the MTFs actually experience, and show how said experiences play a part in the rest of the story.</p>
<p>- as a quick second note, it feels out of character for the Foundation to continue expeditions when personnel are imminent danger, the Foundation would need a strong reason to continue expeditions when they know personnel are likely to be killed.</p>
<p><strong>Red or green?</strong><br />
Due to my afore mentioned concerns, no greenlight.</p>
<p>If you would like me review this (or any concept) further, then please feel free to send me a PM or ask via IRC. Response times generally range from 2-12 hours over PMs. If your looking for additional critiques in general, then I would highly recommend contacting the butterfly squad :)</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>Cheers,</p>
<p>-RED</p>

