			<div class="content" id="post-content-4847502">
									

<p>I don't mean to be harsh but the phrasing in the elevator pitch has me very confused. How would one look at a compas from 200 meters away? How big is this compass?</p>
<p>moreover, it feels a bit like a run of the mill &quot;other dimension&quot; exploration&#8230; I think what you need to do is add some character to both the other dimension and those who are going to be trapped there. What sort of story do you wanna play with here? is there a theme you're working with (other than, alternate universes)?</p>
<p>Keep in mind, the sky is the limit with anomalies and alternative universes&#8230; so what can you do to make this one stand out?</p>
<p>Additionally I would simplify the logic of how people are transported to this other dimension. Also You don't need to designate an observer as part of the SCP unless they're somehow changed. You could just say &quot;individuals observing SCP-XXXX&quot;</p>

